WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:06.120
Hello! In the last lesson we learnt what periods are.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:12.322
Today we will learn how to stay clean during those days.

00:00:13.022 --> 00:00:16.884
Good hygiene protects you from infection,

00:00:16.884 --> 00:00:23.102
itching and odour, and lets you go about your day with confidence.

00:00:23.802 --> 00:00:32.850
Sanitary pads are easy to find. Government Jan Aushadhi Kendras also sell them at a very low price.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.220
Clean cotton cloth pads are also safe,

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.662
as long as they are washed and dried properly.

00:00:42.362 --> 00:00:48.391
A menstrual cup is made of silicone and can last for years.

00:00:48.391 --> 00:00:52.274
Whatever you choose, it must be clean.

00:00:52.974 --> 00:00:59.228
The most important rule: change your pad every four to six hours.

00:00:59.228 --> 00:01:03.462
Keeping one pad on too long lets germs grow.

00:01:04.162 --> 00:01:08.530
This rule applies even on days when the flow is light.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:15.758
Wash a cloth pad first in cold water, then thoroughly with soap.

00:01:16.458 --> 00:01:23.865
Don't hide it to dry in the dark. Direct sunlight kills germs,

00:01:23.865 --> 00:01:27.090
so dry it fully in the sun.

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:33.886
Once dry, keep it in a clean bag in a dry place.

00:01:34.586 --> 00:01:40.178
Always wash your hands with soap before and after changing a pad.

00:01:40.878 --> 00:01:44.709
Wash the genital area with plain water,

00:01:44.709 --> 00:01:50.406
and always clean from front to back so germs don't spread.

00:01:51.106 --> 00:01:56.094
Don't use harsh soap, antiseptic or perfume inside.

00:01:56.094 --> 00:02:00.202
The body keeps itself clean on the inside.

00:02:00.902 --> 00:02:04.889
Wrap a used pad in newspaper or paper,

00:02:04.889 --> 00:02:08.246
and put it in a covered dustbin.

00:02:08.946 --> 00:02:15.474
Never flush a pad down the toilet. It blocks the drains.

00:02:16.174 --> 00:02:21.784
So remember: change pads on time, dry cloth pads in the sun,

00:02:21.784 --> 00:02:25.150
and never forget to wash your hands.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:30.116
If you have itching, burning or a bad smell,

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:35.642
don't feel shy: see a doctor. Now get ready for the quiz!
